From 92da30628cd004ed89e1e65d5fcbe520a5390cba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:17:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B70: queue messages during research turns; deliver batched
 travel previews

On 2026-10-08 a product question sent two minutes into a Tucson travel turn
was steered into it (busy_input_mode: steer). The model then batched the
travel runner with a vacuum search and extract, and answered the vacuum
question from the travel-locked session. The travel controller had passed and
written a receipt, but its preview was never delivered.

- Gateway: while the running turn is on the travel, product or generic
  research route, steer and interrupt are demoted to queue, like the existing
  subagent and compression demotions. /stop and /new still cancel. The busy
  acknowledgement says the message is queued, and that a different request
  needs /new once the run finishes.
- Travel delivery: the approval preview and the controller boundary are found
  when other tool calls are batched with the one controller call. The preview
  is still hash-verified. Two controller calls in one batch are still
  rejected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
